Find the missing limits in the repeated integral below

[MATH: \displaystyle \iiint \limits_{R} f(x,y,z) \: \textrm{d}V
=
\int_{\ast}^{\ast}
\int_{\ast}^{\ast}
\int_{\ast}^{\ast}
f(x,y,z) \: \mathrm{d}y \: \mathrm{d}z \: \mathrm{d}x]
where [MATH: R] is the type III region defined as
[MATH: R=\left\{ (x,y,z) \: : \: -3 \leq x \leq 3, \: x \leq z \leq 2x+2, \: 0 \leq y \leq z+xz \right\}.]
